  "result": "Perfect! All 101 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**Line Discounts Feature**\n\n\u2705 **src/invoices.js updates:**\n- Added `isValidDiscount()` to validate discount percentages (0-100, numeric)\n- New `lineDiscount(line)` function: calculates discount as `lineTotal * discountPercent / 100`, rounded with `roundCents()`\n- Updated `createInvoice()`: accepts optional `discountPercent` on each line (defaults to 0)\n- Updated `addLine()`: accepts optional `discountPercent` with same validation\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()`: now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }` where:\n  - `subtotal` = sum of line totals\n  - `discount` = sum of line discounts\n  - `total` = subtotal - discount, clamped at 0 (no negative totals)\n\n\u2705 **src/render.js updates:**\n- Now displays `Subtotal: \u20acamount` on invoices\n- Shows `Discount: -\u20acamount` only when discount > 0\n- Total line always shown last\n- All amounts formatted via `formatEuros()`\n\n\u2705 **src/errors.js:**\n- Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID`: \"Discount must be a number between 0 and 100.\"\n\n\u2705 **Comprehensive tests (32 new tests):**\n- Discount validation (boundary values, decimal percentages, invalid inputs)\n- Discount calculations with rounding\n- Invoice totals with single/multiple lines and mixed discounts\n- Total clamping at 0 when discount \u2265 subtotal\n- Render output format with discount lines\n- Line counts verified with new summary lines\n\nAll decimal discount percentages (12.5) work correctly, and no amount ever goes below zero. 101 tests passing.",
